  "description": "Intraoperative recordings from a single Neuropixels 1.0 silicon probe (384 sites) inserted into human cortex during neurosurgery at Massachusetts General Hospital. The dataset includes three participants with one task-free recording each, from prefrontal cortex during DBS lead implantation and anterior temporal lobe during lobectomy. This iEEG-BIDS representation contains only the local-field-potential band (0.5-500 Hz, 2.5 kHz), converted losslessly from DANDI NWB files.",
  "methods_description": "Recordings were acquired with SpikeGLX using Neuropixels 1.0 probes, with the LF band band-pass filtered at 0.5-500 Hz and sampled at 2.5 kHz. Reference and ground were sterile needle electrodes in nearby muscle or scalp. The NWB LFP int16 samples were written unchanged to BrainVision files with a resolution of 4.6875 µV per bit.",
